# Member summary and history

Implement a clear MP summary page and a separate full declaration history page. User explicitly removed CSV export and in-app pattern analysis. Summary needs compact identity, all-stored-history known monetary totals per currency, understandable category breakdown visualization, and recent donations/support. History needs all declarations with Svelte-side registration date filters and client-side pagination, filtering before paging. Retain native links, search context, empty/error states and exact amounts.

Grounding. Current frontend App reads route once and renders EntityDetails. Member view displays identity then latest 20 all-category declarations. Existing detail TS parser uses unknown at boundary and exact decimal strings. Service member asks repository member(id, 20); repo repeatable-read profile/count/declaration window left joins funding occurrences, preserving duplicates and empty declarations. No member summaries. Funder detail already groups exact aggregates by known currency with missing-amount/currency coverage. Categories have source numeric IDs and names in DB but only names in DTO. Source labels include employment, donations/other support including loans, gifts, visits, miscellaneous. Domain currently has no useful declaration category enum. No serving receipt date, registration date sufficient. No schema migrations should be needed.

Investigate types/contracts before sketch. Compare whole shapes, including one complete member dataset summarized in domain versus summary and complete-history endpoints. Need canonical typed donation scope based on source category IDs, no duplicated string rules. Choose precise category policy from real data without hiding unrecognized source categories. Keep amount normalization consistent existing funder. Recent donations filter before taking limit. Full summary must not sum recent subset. Any visualization should compute ratios safely without float-based financial summation, keep negatives visible and missing totals distinct from zero.

UI existing visual identity is black/white, Manrope, purple member accents and teal funder accents. Improve hierarchy in existing palette; no unrelated redesign. Desktop funding overview/breakdown, mobile stacked with values wrap. A simple horizontal bar category comparison with exact textual values is preferable to a decorative donut if semantics require signed amounts.

Deliver design candidate only in assigned /tmp directory. Caller usage first, module/type/signature sketch, rationale template, tradeoffs and tests. No implementation, no edits in repo, no agents. Read architect skill and runner-prompt before output. Keep package concise ~100 lines. All paths relative repo at /Users/jamie/development/exposed-member-summary-20261012.
## Usage (caller’s view)

```rust
// HTTP: one consistent member read serves both summary and full history views.
let details = state.entity_details_service.member(id).await?;
Ok(ApiSuccess::new(StatusCode::OK, MemberDetailsResponse::from(details)))
// Service: repository has no presentation limit or donation predicate.
let record = self.repo.member_record(id).await?.ok_or(EntityDetailsError::NotFound)?;
Ok(summarize_member(record))
```
```ts
const state = await loadDetails({ kind: "member", id }, signal);
// /members/:id renders details.summary; /members/:id/history renders all declarations.
const filtered = details.declarations.filter(d => matchesRegistrationDate(d, range));
const visible = filtered.slice((page - 1) * pageSize, page * pageSize);
```

## Problem

The current repository limits declarations to 20 before the service sees them. Neither an exact all-history overview nor complete client-side history filtering can be derived from that window. The existing service/repository/DTO boundaries, funding occurrence multiplicity, decimal strings and native navigation should survive; the window should not.

## Shape

```rust
// domain/models/declaration.rs: replace the empty enum with the canonical source vocabulary.
pub enum DeclarationCategory {
    AdHocEmployment, OngoingEmployment, DonationsAndSupport, UkGifts,
    OverseasVisits, OverseasGifts, LandAndProperty, Shareholdings,
    Miscellaneous, FamilyEmployed, FamilyLobbying, Employment,
    Unrecognized(SourceCategoryId),
}
impl DeclarationCategory {
    pub fn from_source_id(id: SourceCategoryId) -> Self { todo!() }
    pub fn source_id(&self) -> SourceCategoryId { todo!() }
    pub fn is_donation_support(&self) -> bool { todo!() } // exhaustive match
}
// SourceCategoryId parses positive integers at the repository boundary.
// Unrecognized is a valid source-data state, not an unknown closed-enum spelling.
// Keep the source name alongside the category; do not replace it with a guessed label.
pub struct DeclarationRecord {
    pub source_id: i32, pub category: DeclarationCategory, pub category_name: String,
    pub registered_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>, pub entries: Vec<DeclaredFunding>,
}
pub struct MemberRecord { pub member: MemberProfile, pub declarations: Vec<DeclarationRecord> }
pub struct FundingTotal {
    pub amount: Option<BigDecimal>, pub entry_count: i64, pub unknown_amount_count: i64,
}
pub struct CategoryTotal {
    pub category: DeclarationCategory, pub category_name: String, pub total: FundingTotal,
}
pub struct MemberCurrencyTotal {
    pub currency: String, pub total: FundingTotal, pub categories: Vec<CategoryTotal>,
}
pub struct MemberSummary {
    pub currencies: Vec<MemberCurrencyTotal>, pub entry_count: i64,
    pub unknown_currency_count: i64, pub recent_donations: Vec<DeclarationRecord>,
}
pub struct MemberDetails {
    pub member: MemberProfile, pub declarations: Vec<DeclarationRecord>, pub summary: MemberSummary,
}
// domain/repositories/entity_details.rs; replace member(id, recent_limit).
fn member_record(&self, id: MemberId)
    -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<MemberRecord>, EntityDetailsRepoError>> + Send;
// domain/services/entity_details.rs; existing service API stays member(id).
fn summarize_member(record: MemberRecord) -> MemberDetails { todo!() }
```

Stored data checked directly: IDs 1–12 correspond, in order, to the variants above. ID 3 is exactly “Donations and other support (including loans) for activities as an MP”. Recent donations/support uses only that variant; gifts and visits retain their own categories. The overview is explicitly “Known recorded amounts across all declarations”, covering every category, not labelled a donations total. Unknown IDs remain visible with their source name, but are not silently classified as donations.

The repository retains its repeatable-read profile/declarations transaction, removes LIMIT, selects category_id, and preserves the left joins and e.id ordering. Stable order remains registration DESC NULLS LAST, source ID DESC, entry ID. Count comes from the resulting complete declarations, removing a redundant count query and window metadata. No migration is necessary; SQL uses sqlx macros and refreshed offline metadata.

Summary uses a BTreeMap keyed by normalized currency, then source category ID and recorded source name. All occurrences contribute once, including duplicates and negative amounts. No occurrence is created for a left-joined empty declaration. Totals start None and become Some only after a known amount; exact zero is distinct from unknown. Currency trimming uses the existing CURRENCY_WHITESPACE constant in the member SQL projection as it does for funder aggregation; no copied Rust/JS currency normalization. Null/blank currency occurrences contribute to unknown_currency_count, never a fake currency total. Unknown-amount counts are retained per currency/category. Summary scans the complete dataset; recent_donations is category-filtered first and then takes five in repository order.

This is a deep member(id) interface: it owns completeness, scope, exact aggregation and recent-selection policy while callers choose a page. It exposes neither SQL windows nor aggregation stages. Boundary parsing stays in the repository and TS response parser; domain rules stay in the category enum and service.

## Module plan

- `domain/models/declaration.rs`: category identity and classification; no mirrored ID lists in SQL, handlers or TS.
- `domain/models/entity_details.rs`: rename RecentDeclaration, add member summary records, remove bounded-member metadata.
- `domain/repositories/entity_details.rs`, `outbound/entity_details.rs`: one complete consistent MemberRecord read; existing funder path retained.
- `domain/services/entity_details.rs`: pure exact summary and recent donation selection; no second member service endpoint.
- `inbound/http/handlers/entity_details.rs`: decimal strings, numeric category_id plus category_name; serialize summary and history together. Canonical enum performs ID conversion.
- `frontend/src/lib/entity-details.ts`: parse new contract from unknown, reuse declaration reader, add member-history route kind/view and shared member endpoint loading. History length is its total count.
- `frontend/src/MemberSummary.svelte`, `MemberHistory.svelte`: focused views; `EntityDetails.svelte` retains shared load/error/profile behavior and delegates. `App.svelte` accepts the new route. Native links preserve q/strictness between summary, history and search.
- Registration bounds compare UTC YYYY-MM-DD inclusively. Null dates remain visible without bounds and are excluded with active bounds; explain this beside filters. Invalid/reversed bounds show a field error. Filter changes reset page; empty results remain distinct from an empty register.
- Currency sections show exact textual values and horizontal signed bars with a common zero baseline. Calculate relative widths from decimal coefficients using BigInt and an integer 0–10000 ratio; only bounded ratios become JS numbers. Scale by maximum absolute category amount, not signed net total. Unknown totals have no bar and an explicit unavailable label. Mobile stacks labels and wraps amounts.

## Tradeoffs accepted

We accept sending the full member dataset to the summary view in exchange for one consistent read contract and no duplicated aggregate SQL/category policy. A five-item recent subset duplicates a bounded amount of payload to keep selection policy entirely in the service. If measured payload becomes excessive, preserve the complete repository read and split DTO endpoints later; no speculative cache.

## Alternatives considered

Separate summary and full-history endpoints hide payload size but add two handlers, loaders and service paths, and either duplicate repository reads or introduce SQL classification/aggregation ownership. They are justified by measured size, not the current requirement. A frontend-only summary avoids Rust summary records but moves financial arithmetic and domain selection into JS and invites divergent rules; rejected.

## Synthesis decision / implementation reconciliation

Candidate only; no synthesis or implementation decisions yet. No repository changes made.

## Risks and verification

Can a future import change the meaning of an existing source category ID? Current stored mapping is authoritative for this design; unknown IDs stay visible. Verify with fixtures exceeding 20 declarations, late recent donations separated by newer non-donations, duplicate occurrences, empty declarations, missing and blank currencies, missing amounts, mixed currencies, exact fractional cancellation and negative totals. Assert direct HTTP DTO parses through the frontend reader and that date filtering happens before pagination. Capture desktop/mobile summary and history screenshots from the running branch, attach them to the PR, and inspect rendered attachments.

## Next implementation step

Replace the empty category model and bounded repository member read, then implement the pure summary over the complete MemberRecord.
# Member summary and history: one complete member read

## Usage (caller's view)
```rust
// Existing handler keeps one member read; HTTP DTOs stay in inbound/http.
let details = state.entity_details_service.member(id).await?;
Ok(ApiSuccess::new(StatusCode::OK, MemberDetailsResponse::from(details)))
// Service receives a complete consistent stored dataset and owns all summaries.
let history = repo.member_history(id).await?.ok_or(EntityDetailsError::NotFound)?;
let details = summarize_member(history); // exact totals plus recent support
```
```ts
// Both native URLs use the existing loader, with abort/error/identity checks.
const route = readDetailRoute('/members/123/history');
const state = await loadDetails(route, signal);
// Summary displays server-derived summary and recentSupport; history uses all declarations.
const filtered = filterRegistrations(state.details.declarations, from, to);
const visible = filtered.slice((page - 1) * pageSize, page * pageSize);
```

## Problem
The present member repository limits declarations before service policy can inspect them.
The summary therefore cannot be built from its result, and category-name matching would
repeat source classification in SQL, Rust, and Svelte. Two separate pages need complete
stored-history accounting, exact values, and a common identity while preserving empty
records, duplicate occurrences, funder links, and search context.

## Shape
```rust
// domain/models/declaration.rs replaces the unused empty category enum.
// Match authoritative source IDs exactly; names remain source-owned display text.
pub enum DeclarationCategory {
    DonationsAndSupport, Other(SourceCategoryId),
}
pub struct SourceCategoryId(i32); // positive stored/source integer at boundary
impl DeclarationCategory {
    pub fn from_source_id(id: SourceCategoryId) -> Self { todo!() } // 3 => support; all others retained
    pub fn is_donation_or_support(&self) -> bool { todo!() } // exhaustive match
}
pub struct StoredCategory {
    pub kind: DeclarationCategory,
    pub name: String, // keep actual label, including unknown IDs
}
// domain/models/entity_details.rs; rename RecentDeclaration everywhere.
pub struct MemberDeclaration {
    pub source_id: i32, pub category: StoredCategory,
    pub registered_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>, pub entries: Vec<DeclaredFunding>,
}
pub struct MemberHistory { pub member: MemberProfile, pub declarations: Vec<MemberDeclaration> }
pub struct KnownTotal {
    pub amount: Option<BigDecimal>, pub entry_count: i64, pub unknown_amount_count: i64,
}
pub struct CategoryTotal { pub category: StoredCategory, pub total: KnownTotal }
pub struct MemberCurrencyTotal {
    pub currency: String, pub total: KnownTotal, pub categories: Vec<CategoryTotal>,
}
pub struct MemberSummary {
    pub currencies: Vec<MemberCurrencyTotal>, pub entry_count: i64,
    pub unknown_currency_count: i64,
}
pub struct MemberDetails {
    pub history: MemberHistory, pub summary: MemberSummary,
    pub recent_support: Vec<MemberDeclaration>, pub recent_support_limit: usize,
}
// domain/repositories/entity_details.rs removes member(id, recent_limit).
fn member_history(&self, id: MemberId)
    -> impl Future<Output=Result<Option<MemberHistory>, EntityDetailsRepoError>> + Send;
// domain/services/entity_details.rs retains the public member(id) method.
fn summarize_member(history: MemberHistory) -> MemberDetails { todo!() }
```
`member_history` reads identity and every declaration in one repeatable-read transaction,
using SQLx macros and the existing left join/grouping logic without LIMIT. Order remains
registration descending/null-last, source ID descending, occurrence ID ascending. Counts
come from the complete vector; a funding-less declaration remains a declaration.
Summation adds every occurrence with both amount and normalized nonempty currency into
BigDecimal; total `None` means no known amount, whereas exact cancellation yields zero.
Group by source category ID, retaining unknown IDs and original labels. Currency policy
must match funder whitespace normalization exactly; reuse a private adapter helper/value
rather than introduce a second trim rule. Raw entry currency remains available for history.
Recent support filters the complete ordered declarations through the canonical enum before
taking 20; gifts/visits/employment stay in totals and history, not this donations section.

The existing HTTP member response becomes `{member, declarations, summary, recent_support,
recent_support_limit}`; each declaration carries source category ID/name, never a client
classification list. Serialize BigDecimal with existing normalized plain-string conversion.
Remove obsolete declaration_limit, update its consumers and tests in the same change.
TS `MemberDetails` mirrors the response through existing unknown-boundary parsers; its
`Declaration` interface is shared by full history and recent support. No client summation.

`App.svelte` adds member-history route; `EntityDetails.svelte` retains shared identity/funder
view and delegates to `MemberSummary.svelte` / `MemberHistory.svelte`. Native summary/history
anchors preserve q/strictness. History date inputs use UTC registration calendar dates,
inclusive start/end; undated declarations appear only with no active date bounds. Reset
page when bounds change. Invalid/reversed ranges show a clear inline error. Empty filtered
results differ from no stored declarations. No category filter, export, or analysis feature.

Summary shows separate currency totals and signed horizontal category bars with exact
text values. A small pure decimal-string-to-scaled-BigInt helper computes bounded visual
widths relative to max absolute category amount; convert only the final 0–1000 ratio to
Number. Show negative bars/signs, explicit unavailable amounts, and missing-currency count.

## Synthesis decision
Candidate recommendation: one complete domain read and one endpoint shared by two pages.

## Tradeoffs accepted
- Accept downloading complete history on the summary page for one consistent simple API.
- Accept transient recent-support clones for an explicit server-owned filtered subset.
- Accept no historical-party inference or currency conversion; labels describe stored history.

## Alternatives considered
- Separate summary/history endpoints: hides payload size but duplicates read/query paths and
  requires a second DTO/loader outcome. Worth revisiting only with measured payload pressure.
- SQL aggregates plus bounded category-filtered recent query: hides data volume but repeats
  category and normalization policy between SQL and domain unless passed derived enum IDs.
  Requires more repository contracts and grouping logic than this dataset currently needs.

## Implementation reconciliation
Design only; no implementation deviations accepted.

## Open questions and risks
The live category query supplied by the orchestrator establishes ID 3 as donations/other
support including loans; IDs 1/2/12 are employment, 4 UK gifts, 5 visits, 6 overseas gifts,
7 land/property, 8 shares, 9 miscellaneous, 10 family employment, 11 family lobbying.
These other IDs stay `Other(id)` rather than pretending this is a closed upstream vocabulary.
Should loans be labelled explicitly in explanatory text? Preserve their category 3 scope.

## Next implementation step
Implement ID 3 classification, then replace the bounded repository read and category placeholder.

## Verification
Test >20 declarations with old donations after recent employment; summary includes all.
Test duplicate occurrences, empty declarations, unknown categories/currencies, missing amounts,
negative amounts, zero cancellation, large fractional decimals, and whitespace normalization.
Test date filtering before pagination and page reset, UTC boundaries, null dates, and reversed
bounds. Capture desktop/mobile summary and history screenshots from the running branch.
## Problem

A member page currently returns a bounded latest-declaration window, so it cannot truthfully show lifetime totals or power a full history view. Declaration `category_id` is stored beside its source name, but the domain has no classification; the same ID-to-policy rule must drive the donation summary and recent-support slice. Preserve exact `BigDecimal` sums, unknown amounts/currencies, duplicate funding occurrences, empty declarations, stable registration ordering, and the existing API's separate wire DTO boundary. No schema change is needed.

## Usage (caller's view)

The summary page loads one compact response:

```ts
const summary = await loadMemberSummary(id, signal);
// summary.totalsByCurrency[0].amount is an exact decimal string or null.
// summary.recentSupport contains the newest six category-3 declarations.
```

The separate history route loads the full record set, then filters before slicing pages:

```ts
const history = await loadMemberHistory(id, signal);
const filtered = history.declarations.filter(d => inDateRange(d.registeredAt, range));
const page = filtered.slice(pageIndex * pageSize, (pageIndex + 1) * pageSize);
```

A declaration renders every occurrence and uses the stored source category name, including unknown category IDs. Existing search context, not-found, loading and error behavior remain shared.

## Shape

Use two endpoints with domain-owned summary/history operations. This keeps the summary payload bounded while allowing the history screen to render every declaration without pagination requests or server-filter semantics. Both reads use a repeatable-read transaction, so each individual response is internally consistent.

```rust
// domain/models/declaration_category.rs
pub enum DeclarationCategory {
    AdHocEmployment, OngoingEmployment, DonationsAndOtherSupport,
    UkGifts, Visits, OverseasGifts, LandAndProperty, Shareholdings,
    Miscellaneous, FamilyEmployed, FamilyLobbying, Employment,
    Other(u32),
}
impl DeclarationCategory {
    pub fn from_source_id(id: u32) -> Self; // exhaustive ID mapping; 3 is donation/support
    pub fn is_donation_or_support(&self) -> bool; // true only for that variant
}
```

`Other(id)` retains new/future categories. The mapping is the sole owner of source-ID policy; SQL and TypeScript do not keep an ID allowlist. The source category name stays alongside the enum for display, not classification.

```rust
// domain/models/entity_details.rs
pub struct MemberSummary {
    pub member: MemberProfile,
    pub totals_by_currency: Vec<CurrencyTotal>, // all stored occurrences, all categories
    pub category_totals: Vec<CategoryCurrencyTotal>, // category ID/name + currency + exact optional total + coverage
    pub recent_support: Vec<RecentDeclaration>, // newest six category-3 declarations
    pub declaration_count: i64,
}
pub struct CurrencyTotal { pub currency: String, pub amount: Option<BigDecimal>,
    pub entry_count: i64, pub unknown_amount_count: i64 }
pub struct CategoryCurrencyTotal { pub category_id: u32, pub category_name: String,
    pub currency: Option<String>, pub amount: Option<BigDecimal>,
    pub entry_count: i64, pub unknown_amount_count: i64 }
pub struct MemberHistory { pub member: MemberProfile, pub declarations: Vec<RecentDeclaration> }
```

`None` total means no known amount; an exact zero remains zero. Unknown currency is represented as a `None` currency category-total bucket and omitted from known-currency totals, with counts retained. Keep category rows separate by source ID and name so labels and new categories are never collapsed. The chart groups by currency and uses signed horizontal bars (negative values extend left); exact text values remain authoritative. Compute bar widths from decimal magnitudes after finding the largest absolute value, without converting or summing money through floating point.

```rust
// domain/repositories/entity_details.rs
fn member_summary(&self, id: MemberId, support_limit: usize)
 -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<MemberSummary>, EntityDetailsRepoError>> + Send;
fn member_history(&self, id: MemberId)
 -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<MemberHistory>, EntityDetailsRepoError>> + Send;

// domain/services/entity_details/interface.rs
fn member_summary(&self, id: MemberId)
 -> impl Future<Output = Result<MemberSummary, EntityDetailsError>> + Send;
fn member_history(&self, id: MemberId)
 -> impl Future<Output = Result<MemberHistory, EntityDetailsError>> + Send;
```

The service owns the six-item recent-support limit and converts missing identities to `NotFound`. The summary repository aggregates at `(category_id, category_name, normalized currency)` and `(currency)` granularity in SQL using `sqlx` macros and exact `NUMERIC` sums; summary query joins each declaration to funding rows once and counts occurrences, avoiding join fanout. It selects latest support declarations by category ID before applying `LIMIT`, then left-joins entries so empty declarations survive. History reads every declaration and its funding occurrences in stable registration-date/source-ID/entry-ID order, also left-joined. Both reuse a private row-to-domain conversion for timestamps, exact values, and duplicate preservation.

HTTP handler additions expose `GET /api/members/{id}/summary` and `GET /api/members/{id}/declarations`, with distinct response DTOs in the existing `entity_details` handler module. Serialize amounts with `normalized().to_plain_string()`. The summary DTO includes category IDs, names, counts, currency, totals, recent declarations and member profile; the history DTO includes profile and complete declarations. TypeScript adds validated `MemberSummary`/`MemberHistory` parsers in `frontend/src/lib/entity-details.ts`; retain decimal strings and IDs as strings. Add `DetailRoute` member subroute for `/members/:id/declarations`, render summary and history as separate Svelte components or route branches in `EntityDetails.svelte`, preserving current back-to-search parameters and states.

The interface is intentionally two reads: one bounded summary operation hides aggregation and category policy; one full history operation exposes only the full record set. The UI does filtering and pagination because the requested filters are client-side and this payload is the screen's full source. No transport types leak into domain models.

## Synthesis decision

Candidate recommends two distinct read shapes: a bounded, pre-aggregated summary and an unbounded declaration history. This avoids transferring all history just to show summary totals while keeping client filtering straightforward.

## Tradeoffs accepted

- We accept one additional API request for the history page in exchange for a small summary response and independent page loading.
- We accept full-history transfer and browser memory proportional to a member's declarations in exchange for exact client-side date filtering and pagination.
- We accept a Rust enum with an `Other(u32)` case in exchange for one canonical donation rule and forward compatibility.
- We accept repeating the profile in history responses in exchange for independently loadable route state.
- We accept category/currency rows even when a total is unavailable in exchange for distinguishing missing data from zero and retaining coverage.

## Alternatives considered

- One endpoint returning all declarations plus derived summary: simple backend interface, but exposes unbounded transfer and forces summary callers to pay for history; rejected on payload/interface depth.
- Two endpoints where history is server-paginated and filtered: hides transfer size but exposes query/filter/page protocol to the UI and cannot meet the stated client-filterable full-history behavior; rejected.
- Frontend-only aggregation from all history: fewer Rust summary types, but transfers every occurrence to the summary and duplicates exact aggregation policy in TypeScript; rejected.

## Implementation reconciliation

No implementation changes accepted yet.

## Open questions and risks

- Should category breakdown rows include zero-entry categories from source taxonomy, or only categories represented by stored declarations? This design uses represented categories.
- Can one member's history exceed practical browser memory? If so, that changes the explicit client-filterable/full-history requirement and should trigger a revised contract.

## Next implementation step

Add the canonical `DeclarationCategory` mapping and the summary/history domain models, then wire repository queries and DTOs to those types.

